# The `test-result` tool (SPEC, "Tools"): the bash worker image with this
# directory's script curried onto it, plus the `help` the agent registers it by.
#
# The docs are a HERE-STRING, so they live in the `.caos-expr` — which is
# STRIPPED from the tree the expression is evaluated against. Editing them
# re-keys this tool's arg tree and nothing else: no build sees these bytes.
HELP=<<END
Print one test's COMPLETE record from a `test` run: the test's whole output —
the report only carries its last few lines — or, with `log`, one of the inner
stack's logs. Takes the hash the test report prints beside each test's name;
that hash is stable, so the record of a run stays readable long after the run.
@param hash The hash the `test` report prints beside a test's name.
@param [log] Print this inner-stack log instead of the test's output: server, runnerd, redis or serve.
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --worker1:@=worker.sh --help=$HELP
